{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/991131-embracing-the-wyrd-how-do-you-go-owa","id":991131,"title":"Embracing the Wyrd: how do you go OWA?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T14:47:22-07:00","id":991131,"title":"Embracing the Wyrd: how do you go OWA?","content":"Who else is having fun making up Embrace Forms for all their old characters?<br /> <br /> And now I totally want to make an ogre or elemental, whose durance involved a lot of anime tropes, who normally has a huge, hulking appearance but gets much smaller and more streamlined when they Embrace The Wyrd (<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BishonenLine\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BishonenLine</a>).<br /> <br /> Actually, I have an idea for that: a gristlegrinder whose Embrace represents them &quot;digesting&quot; all their own food and fat for a supercharged burst of energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:48:57-07:00","id":991194,"title":"","content":"I've given thought to the idea of letting my players add personal mechanical quirks to Embracing. If you've got high enough Wyrd, it's supposed to be a brief, crazy power trip. One of my powerful NPCs, Ziggy Zapf, Sorcerer of Autumn, Gremlin/Gameplayer kith, working as a game developer, winds up seeing combat as turn-based (sorry about the broken fourth wall, there) when he Embraces, and he gets to cheat: He doesn't operate on the usual initiative order. When someone declares their action, Ziggy can choose to shove his turn in front of theirs. In terms of appearance, he basically gets his own version of Transistor's Turn():<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N2Awskq-y8M\" data-code=\"N2Awskq-y8M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/N2Awskq-y8M/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Mortals wind up shifting between being frozen helpless, or in super slow-mo, watching Ziggy plan out the optimal response, and then watching him effortlessly dodge their attacks at supernatural speed once the clock suddenly gets back to ticking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:08:35-07:00","id":991196,"title":"","content":"That is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:48:13-07:00","id":991249,"title":"","content":"I think my fairest mirrorskin will probably have their mein shapechange every turn, making them look like an appropriate character for however the extra dice are being spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:32:34-07:00","id":991558,"title":"","content":"How does Embracing the Wyrd work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:32:22-07:00","id":991591,"title":"","content":"Spend a point of Glamour and a point of willpower to activate it, basically you open yourself up to the full power of the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> You gain bonus dice equal to you wyrd per turn which can be spent on instant actions, defence or resistance traits.<br /> <br /> You can also spend glamour up your maxium per turn to add more bonus dice per turn.<br /> <br /> You also add your Wyrd to speed.<br /> <br /> You risk bewitching mortals who see you.<br /> <br /> Its a Clarity breaking point, with - half your Wyrd to the roll.<br /> <br /> Lastly its filled with unique special effect that make you look cooler embracing the Wyrd, this an RP effect not mechanical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:41:08-07:00","id":991595,"title":"","content":"got it. Like Goku's first time going Super Saiyan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:43